    "title": "Yorkville Softball Rolls Behind Fox's Complete-Game Effort - Tuesday's Sports Recap - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By wspy_sports ,\n13 hours ago Yorkville’s dominant softball victory highlighted Tuesday’s high school varsity action as the Foxes defeated Johnson Central (of Kentucky) 15-3 behind a complete-game performance from Ellie Fox, who allowed three earned runs on six hits with three walks and 11 strikeouts over five innings, while Alyssa Muhlbach led the offense with a triple that drove in three runs along with a double, Taylor Jackson added an inside-the-park home run with two RBIs, Kayla Kersting doubled, drove in two runs and scored twice, Austyn Strike recorded two hits including a double while driving in a run and scoring once, Callie Ferko and Fox each added RBI singles, Alivia Lathan doubled, and Strike also contributed another RBI single. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
